# Collaboration

Commit no secrets, `.env` files, credentials, or provider keys. `.env.example` contains variable names and placeholders only.

The initial bootstrap may land on `main`. After that commit, do the work on a feature branch and open a pull request for review.

Change only what the request requires. Leave unrelated files, dependencies, and refactors untouched. Commit or push only when the user asks.
